{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"sed -n '1,172p' ../investigation/ideas/02_cross_fitted_ilr_residual_geometry/program_1/src/program.py; sed -n '1050,1135p' ../task/evaluate_final.py; sed -n '85,145p' .codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/SKILL.md; head -45 references.bib; ls /opt; ls /usr/bin/apply_patch /usr/local/bin/apply_patch /tmp/apply_patch /tmp/repo_support/apply_patch 2>/dev/null || true\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"sed -n '1,172p' ../investigation/ideas/02_cross_fitted_ilr_residual_geometry/program_1/src/program.py; sed -n '1050,1135p' ../task/evaluate_final.py; sed -n '85,145p' .codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/SKILL.md; head -45 references.bib; ls /opt; ls /usr/bin/apply_patch /usr/local/bin/apply_patch /tmp/apply_patch /tmp/repo_support/apply_patch 2>/dev/null || true\"","aggregated_output":"\"\"\"Training-only boundary-adaptive ILR ellipsoid predictor, finite JSON RPC v1.\n\nAll operations return EXACTLY the keys described here; extra keys are forbidden.\nNo paths, metrics, test targets, calibration responses, or plane identity are inputs.\nSeeds initialize randomness only; accept any nonnegative signed-64-bit integer seed.\nreset {op,seed} -> {ok:true}: discard model and both in-memory transfer buffers.\n\nfit_start {op,n_rows,composition_dim,ilr_basis,alpha,nbytes,chunks} -> {ok:true}:\none training phase per reset; 1<=n_rows<=4096, K=composition_dim in {3,8},\nalpha=0.1, ilr_basis is K by K-1 orthonormal contrast matrix. Training consists\nof row-major float64 X[n_rows,5], then Y[n_rows,K] (positive, row sums one).\nnbytes=8*n_rows*(5+K), chunks=ceil(nbytes/1048576), at most four chunks.\nfit_chunk {op,index,block} -> {ok:true}: consecutive zero-based indices only.\nfit_commit {op} -> {ok:true}: require all bytes; fit actual predictor, free upload.\nAll training inputs are authorized; calibration is performed by the evaluator.\n\npredict_start {op,x:block} -> {n_rows,dimension,nbytes,chunks,encoding,dtype,shape}:\nrequires committed fit and no live prediction. X has shape [N,5], 1<=N<=5952.\nReturn dimension d=K-1; buffer is row-major float64 [N,d+d*d], location first,\nthen a FULL row-major lower triangular Cholesky factor of a positive shape.\nshape=[N,d+d*d], encoding='base64', dtype='<f8', nbytes=8*N*(d+d*d),\nchunks=ceil(nbytes/1048576)<=4. A prediction must be a fixed row-wise function\nof X after fit: no test-time updating, batch position, or batch-size dependence.\npredict_chunk {op,index} -> {block}: ordered chunks of flattened output.\npredict_release {op} -> {ok:true}: requires all chunks read; erase output buffer.\nThe evaluator performs three prediction transfers: full authorized query batch,\nreordered query subset, and another subset, without revealing partition boundaries.\n\nEvery block has EXACT keys {encoding,dtype,shape,nbytes,data}: base64 ASCII data,\nencoding='base64', dtype='<f8', shape a positive integer list, nbytes=8*prod(shape).\nChunk blocks use shape [number_of_float64_values], at most 1048576 raw bytes.\nAll numeric values must be finite. Location and factor magnitudes <=1e6;\nfactor diagonals >=1e-8; singular-value condition number <=1e10.\nAt most 4 MiB per logical buffer, 512 MiB total candidate-owned memory allowed;\ncomplete framed UTF-8 JSON messages <8 MiB (and always <64 MiB). No disk exchange.\nNo optional response keys or candidate diagnostics are supported. Errors are protocol\nfailures, not a channel for scientific self-reports. Reset is the only restart.\nEvaluator controls include matched constant inputs, genuine training derangement,\nactual point-copy singleton/full-simplex membership, query invariance, and replay.\nNeither nominal coverage nor superiority is an eligibility gate: negative results\nare valid when execution and required instrumentation are valid. Search utility is\n1 - .8*max(0,.9-coverage)/.9 - .2*normalized_volume, equally weighted case then seed.\n\"\"\"\nimport base64\nimport math\nimport numpy as np\n\nCHUNK = 1048576\nSTATE = {}\n\n\ndef decode(block):\n    if set(block) != {'encoding', 'dtype', 'shape', 'nbytes', 'data'}:\n        raise ValueError('invalid block')\n    if block['encoding'] != 'base64' or block['dtype'] != '<f8':\n        raise ValueError('invalid encoding')\n    shape = block['shape']\n    if not isinstance(shape, list) or not shape or any(type(size) is not int or size < 1 for size in shape):\n        raise ValueError('invalid shape')\n    size = math.prod(shape) * 8\n    if size != block['nbytes'] or size > 4 * CHUNK:\n        raise ValueError('invalid size')\n    raw = base64.b64decode(block['data'], validate=True)\n    if len(raw) != size:\n        raise ValueError('invalid byte count')\n    array = np.frombuffer(raw, dtype='<f8').reshape(shape)\n    if not np.isfinite(array).all():\n        raise ValueError('nonfinite')\n    return array\n\n\ndef encode(array):\n    array = np.asarray(array, dtype='<f8', order='C')\n    return {'encoding': 'base64', 'dtype': '<f8', 'shape': list(array.shape),\n            'nbytes': array.nbytes, 'data': base64.b64encode(array.tobytes()).decode('ascii')}\n\n\ndef features(covariates):\n    columns = [np.ones(len(covariates))]\n    columns.extend(covariates[:, index] for index in range(5))\n    columns.extend(covariates[:, index] ** 2 for index in range(5))\n    columns.extend(covariates[:, first] * covariates[:, second]\n                   for first in range(5) for second in range(first))\n    return np.column_stack(columns)\n\n\ndef ridge(design, targets, penalty):\n    return np.linalg.solve(design.T @ design + penalty * np.eye(design.shape[1]), design.T @ targets)\n\n\ndef predicted_boundary(means, basis):\n    logits = means @ basis.T\n    weights = np.exp(logits - logits.max(axis=-1, keepdims=True))\n    predictions = weights / weights.sum(axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n    return predictions.min(axis=-1)\n\n\ndef boundary_groups(predicted_boundary_score, boundary_edges):\n    boundary_group = np.searchsorted(boundary_edges, predicted_boundary_score, side='right')\n    return boundary_group\n\n\ndef fit_model(covariates, responses, basis):\n    transformed = np.log(responses) @ basis\n    design = features(covariates)\n    dimension = basis.shape[1]\n    if len(covariates) < 4:\n        location = ridge(design, transformed, 0.01)\n        variance = np.zeros((design.shape[1], dimension))\n        train_boundary_scores = predicted_boundary(design @ location, basis)\n        boundary_edges = np.quantile(train_boundary_scores, [1.0 / 3.0, 2.0 / 3.0])\n        group_factors = np.repeat(np.eye(dimension)[None, :, :], 3, axis=0)\n        return location, variance, boundary_edges, group_factors\n    fold_count = 4\n    fold_ids = np.arange(len(covariates)) % fold_count\n    oof_residuals = np.empty_like(transformed)\n    for fold_index in range(fold_count):\n        held_out = fold_ids == fold_index\n        fold_location = ridge(design[~held_out], transformed[~held_out], 0.01)\n        oof_residuals[held_out] = transformed[held_out] - design[held_out] @ fold_location\n    final_location = ridge(design, transformed, 0.01)\n    variance = ridge(design, np.log(oof_residuals ** 2 + 0.02), 5.0)\n    train_boundary_scores = predicted_boundary(design @ final_location, basis)\n    boundary_edges = np.quantile(train_boundary_scores, [1.0 / 3.0, 2.0 / 3.0])\n    residual_groups = boundary_groups(train_boundary_scores, boundary_edges)\n    scales = np.exp(0.5 * np.clip(design @ variance, -6, 5))\n    standardized = np.clip(oof_residuals / scales, -1000.0, 1000.0)\n    identity = np.eye(dimension)\n    pooled_shape = (standardized.T @ standardized + 8.0 * identity) / (len(oof_residuals) + 8.0)\n    group_factors = np.empty((3, dimension, dimension))\n    for group_index in range(3):\n        group_residuals = standardized[residual_groups == group_index]\n        group_shape = (group_residuals.T @ group_residuals + 32.0 * pooled_shape) / (len(group_residuals) + 32.0)\n        group_factors[group_index] = np.linalg.cholesky(group_shape)\n    return final_location, variance, boundary_edges, group_factors\n\n\ndef handle(request):\n    operation = request['op']\n    if operation == 'reset':\n        if set(request) != {'op', 'seed'} or type(request['seed']) is not int or not 0 <= request['seed'] < 2**63:\n            raise ValueError('invalid reset')\n        STATE.clear()\n        STATE['rng'] = np.random.default_rng(request['seed'])\n        return {'ok': True}\n    if 'rng' not in STATE:\n        raise ValueError('reset required')\n    if operation == 'fit_start':\n        if 'upload' in STATE or 'model' in STATE:\n            raise ValueError('one fit per reset')\n        rows, size = request['n_rows'], request['composition_dim']\n        if type(rows) is not int or not 1 <= rows <= 4096 or size not in (3, 8):\n            raise ValueError('invalid training shape')\n        raw_size = rows * (5 + size) * 8\n        if request['nbytes'] != raw_size or request['chunks'] != math.ceil(raw_size / CHUNK):\n            raise ValueError('invalid transfer')\n        basis = np.asarray(request['ilr_basis'], dtype=float)\n        if basis.shape != (size, size - 1) or not np.allclose(basis.T @ basis, np.eye(size - 1)):\n            raise ValueError('invalid basis')\n        STATE.update(upload=bytearray(), metadata=dict(request), basis=basis, upload_index=0)\n        return {'ok': True}\n    if operation == 'fit_chunk':\n        if 'upload' not in STATE or request['index'] != STATE['upload_index']:\n            raise ValueError('invalid upload order')\n        block = decode(request['block'])\n        expected = min(CHUNK, STATE['metadata']['nbytes'] - len(STATE['upload']))\n        if block.ndim != 1 or block.nbytes != expected or expected < 1:\n            raise ValueError('invalid upload length')\n        STATE['upload'].extend(block.tobytes())\n        STATE['upload_index'] += 1\n        return {'ok': True}\n    if operation == 'fit_commit':\n            for key in ('component', 'category', 'operation')}\n    record['failure'] = safe\n    if PLANE == 'search':\n        print('episode_failure component={component} category={category} operation={operation}'.format(**safe)[:256],\n              file=sys.stderr, flush=True)\n\n\ndef record_secondary_failure(failure, record):\n    safe = {key: bounded_failure_name(failure.get(key), 'unknown')\n            for key in ('component', 'category', 'operation')}\n    record.setdefault('secondary_failures', []).append(safe)\n    if PLANE == 'search':\n        print('episode_secondary_failure component={component} category={category} operation={operation}'.format(**safe),\n              file=sys.stderr, flush=True)\n\n\ndef run_declared_episodes(episodes, *, hard_deadline, finish_reserve, reset_timeout, episode_overhead,\n                          rpc_cap, clock, rpc, evaluate, worst_case, record_failure, cleanup):\n    candidate_deadline = hard_deadline - finish_reserve\n    reset_slot = reset_timeout + episode_overhead\n    outcomes = [worst_case(episode) for episode in episodes]\n    if clock() + len(episodes) * reset_slot > candidate_deadline:\n        raise TimeoutError('insufficient time for declared reset reservations')\n    complete = True\n    for index, episode in enumerate(episodes):\n        began = clock()\n        remaining = len(episodes) - index - 1\n        episode_deadline = candidate_deadline - remaining * reset_slot\n        work_deadline = episode_deadline - episode_overhead\n        current_operation = 'reset'\n        primary_failure = None\n        record = outcomes[index]\n        failed = True\n\n        def retain_failure():\n            nonlocal record\n            retained = worst_case(episode)\n            for key in ('failure', '_failure_emitted', 'worker_failure', 'secondary_failures',\n                        'baseline_productive_seconds'):\n                if key in record:\n                    retained[key] = record[key]\n            outcomes[index] = retained\n            record = retained\n\n        def call(request, *, deadline=None):\n            nonlocal current_operation, primary_failure\n            current_operation = request.get('op', 'unknown')\n            try:\n                timeout = min(rpc_cap, work_deadline - clock(),\n                              (deadline - clock()) if deadline is not None else rpc_cap)\n                if timeout <= 0:\n                    raise TimeoutError('episode work budget exhausted')\n                response = rpc(request, timeout=timeout)\n                if deadline is not None and clock() > deadline:\n                    raise TimeoutError('method work budget exhausted')\n                return response\n            except (TimeoutError, RequiredBaselineFailure, ProtocolError) as error:\n                if primary_failure is None:\n                    primary_failure = describe_episode_failure(error, current_operation)\n                raise\n\n        try:\n            timeout = min(reset_timeout, rpc_cap, work_deadline - clock())\n            if timeout <= 0:\n                raise TimeoutError('episode reset budget exhausted')\n            require_reset_ack(rpc({'op': 'reset', 'seed': episode['seed']}, timeout=timeout))\n            value = evaluate(episode, call, work_deadline, record)\n            if clock() > work_deadline:\n                raise TimeoutError('episode work deadline exceeded')\n            outcomes[index] = value\n            record = value\n            failed = False\n        except (TimeoutError, RequiredBaselineFailure, InvalidResetResponse, ProtocolError) as error:\n            complete = False\n            failure = primary_failure or describe_episode_failure(error, current_operation)\n            retain_failure()\n            record_failure(failure, record)\n        except FatalTransportError as error:\n            complete = False\n            retain_failure()\n            record_failure({'component': 'broker', 'category': 'transport_failure',\n                            'operation': bounded_failure_name(current_operation, 'unknown')}, record)\n            error.outcomes = outcomes\n            raise\n        finally:\n            original = sys.exception()\n  --references references_provenance.json \\\n  --bib references.bib \\\n  --claims claims_grounding.json \\\n  --paper-dir .\n```\nThis validator also checks that `references.bib` and `references_provenance.json` stay in sync, and traces every `@evidence[[...]]` link under `--paper-dir` against the `scientific-evidence/` bundle via the `scientific-evidence` skill verifier. Every link must classify as `resolved` or `anchored`; any `dangling` link is a hard error you must fix before finalization. If paper text carries `@evidence[[...]]` tokens but the bundle is missing, generate it first with `bash ../scientific-evidence/scripts/scientific_evidence.sh emit-bundle --root-dir .`.\n33. During repair passes, also rerun the full `validate-paper` workflow after each fix round so the next round starts from fresh feedback, not stale assumptions.\n34. When venue guidance is present, make the title, abstract, introduction, and conclusion explicitly reader-facing for that venue's scientific questions whenever the grounded evidence supports that framing.\n35. If `./paper_authors.tex` exists, treat it as the canonical author source. Keep `\\input{paper_authors.tex}` inside `\\author{...}` when possible; otherwise copy the exact file contents without edits.\n36. Keep the template's watermark block (`% --- watermark (auto-inserted) ---` … `% --- end watermark ---`) in `paper.tex` unchanged; the orchestrator regenerates it before every host compile.\n\n# Outputs\n- `paper.tex`\n- `claims_grounding.json`\n- `figure_manifest.json` when figures are generated or required by strategy\n- Optional extra figures in `figures/` (grounded only, no cross-agent aggregate plots).\n@Article{Yerke2024ProportionbasedNO,\n author = {Aaron Yerke and Daisy Fry Brumit and Anthony A. Fodor},\n booktitle = {Microbiome},\n journal = {Microbiome},\n title = {Proportion-based normalizations outperform compositional data transformations in machine learning applications},\n volume = {12},\n year = {2024}\n}\n\n@Article{Wang2018RobustVE,\n author = {Zong Wang and Wen-Jiao Shi},\n booktitle = {Geoderma},\n journal = {Geoderma},\n title = {Robu